<h2 id="qwengpu-puts-a-small-parallel-machine-inside-qwen">qwenGPU puts a small parallel machine inside Qwen</h2>

<p>qwenGPU inserts 45 constructed layers ahead of Qwen3.5-2B’s original layers. These implement a four-lane machine in which lanes run instructions together and can take different branches. Registers and memory live in the recurrent state of Gated DeltaNet layers. Generated execution records show which blocks run and which values they produce. <a href="https://github.com/vixhal-baraiya/qwenGPU">qwenGPU repository</a></p>

<p>The host compiles CUDA source to PTX, lowers it to the machine’s supported instructions, loads the program and inputs, and retrieves the output. The added model layers carry out the instructions. The repository reports that its reference interpreter matched a Tesla T4 on 49 test kernels and that checked model launches matched the interpreter. In a separate chat test, Qwen wrote a correct kernel on its first attempt for four of five sampled questions. That distinction matters because exact execution preserves the behavior of whatever program the model supplied, including a mistaken one. <a href="https://github.com/vixhal-baraiya/qwenGPU#results">qwenGPU results</a></p>

